            "review_text": "Helen C\n2 contributions\n0\nGreat food, terrible service. Take a local if you go and maybe they will treat you better.\nDec 2025 • Family\nWent here at the recommendation of our tour director. Everything started out just fine. We were put at a table between 2 pillars. We are English speaking and 1 of the head waiters took our order. We ordered the string beans (phenomenal), the duck (great), a couple of apps (terrific). We were asked if we wanted rice or fried noodles and said fried noodles. You would never have guessed they had wine if you didnt asked. Things were OK at first, we got everything piece meal and after awhile were ignored as we watched all the other tables getting their food. The original waitress showed up and we asked for more wine because we were still waiting on the fried noodles and none of us had drinks anymore. Instead of bringing the wine she came back and asked if we wanted the check. We said we were waiting on the fried noodles and instead of bringing them, they came to the table and argued with us saying if we wanted them we needed to order them. It is unfortunate because the food was good but we left hungry, there were 6 of us, and they lost interest in serving us. Not sure how they became a Michelin restaurant.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten December 17, 2025",
