            "review_text": "Шонни Тхай\nHue, Vietnam303 contributions\n0\nGot food poisoning after this restaurant\nJun 2024 • Solo\nThe location is convenient, right opposite the Sheraton Saigon hotel. From the outside the establishment looks very old and worn out. Came there due to it being recommended as one of the top five restaurants in Ho Chi Minh City for Peking duck. The price for a half of duck on the menu was 450,000 dong, but in the end the bill was issued with VAT in the amount of 510,300 dong. Not as tasty compared to Vietnamese roast duck. And that's not it. I decided never to try such a dish again in such a sanitarily questionable Chinese establishment. Especially after I got seriously poisoned in the evening after a restaurant. I was sick all night and sat on the toilet. Horror!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nShow original\nWritten June 8, 2024",
